    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0371" n="255" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg255"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.543 C 42/6.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Reinsch.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 351.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 8, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Department has received your No. 770 of September 30, 1915, and approves your
                    course in pointing out to the Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs that the case
                    was one between Americans and Chinese in which no other nationality was
                    involved, and requesting for the Legation’s files another statement of the
                    settlement, which should not confuse the question at issue by irrelevant
                    references to third parties.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
